    {
      "block_id": "2605.18130_p6_b28",
      "text": "The final classification logits are predicted by a Multi-\nLayer Perceptron (MLP): Ycls = MLP(Fpool). This multi-\ndimensional fusion strategy compels the classification network\nnot only to focus deeply on the internal echoic structural\ndistribution of the lesion but also to sensitively capture critical\nsurrounding tissue infiltration features essential for ultrasound\nclinical diagnosis (e.g., spiculated margins, posterior acoustic\nshadowing), thereby significantly enhancing the robustness of\nthe classification boundary.\n",
      "bbox": [
        311.98,
        257.15,
        563.04,
        362.75
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        1247,
        1028,
